{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-integral-bound","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0305","math_ordinal":31,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The change of variables covers the normal left tail up to c and the next integral explicitly starts at negative infinity; a positive-infinity lower bound would reverse or empty the intended integral.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt274.tex:79-82","source_normalized_sha256":"aa8026e98bb436190353e4391c3d1010e98d2980882b06408bd7ca967ed3db63","source_text":"\\int_{\\infty}^ce^{-(x-a)^2/2\\sigma^2}dx","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt274.tex:77-80","target_normalized_sha256":"708a949f4d7281d38d38112c3287a1986cd1f533206baf0fe573bd81d7da74bf","target_text":"\\int_{-\\infty}^ce^{-(x-a)^2/2\\sigma^2}dx","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S274"}
{"classification":"mathematical-spurious-scale-denominator","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0306","math_ordinal":60,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"Z_1 and Z_2 were just standardized, so their joint density is the product of two standard-normal densities and contains no sigma_1 sigma_2 scale factor.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt274.tex:128-129","source_normalized_sha256":"0d576e688081adb180e10980a5dae0b65a253d7e301ed24c29abe411fb02f0cb","source_text":"\\Bover1{2\\pi\\sigma_1\\sigma_2}e^{-(\\zeta_1^2+\\zeta_2^2)/2}","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt274.tex:125-126","target_normalized_sha256":"8253e8b8557ab14085231b5cc5264de60222223cfeaebe8e861928a668bcfabe","target_text":"\\Bover1{2\\pi}e^{-(\\zeta_1^2+\\zeta_2^2)/2}","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S274"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-summand-indices","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0307","math_ordinal":91,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"W_j must contain all the other indexed summands so that Z_j=W_j+V_j and Z_{j+1}=W_j+U_j; repeating U_j and V_j does not yield either identity.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt274.tex:184","source_normalized_sha256":"bf3bc7c1b96688ed07e3897455f433e25ffef1b72fba391348eae20baa5d5598","source_text":"$W_j=\\sum_{i=0}^{j-1}U_j+\\sum_{i=j+1}^nV_j$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt274.tex:182","target_normalized_sha256":"060a4d384975a22e0a68e92f972b658f1d747fe4a6b488ae3637afdb3d30b4c1","target_text":"$W_j=\\sum_{i=0}^{j-1}U_i+\\sum_{i=j+1}^nV_i$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S274"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-function-argument","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0308","math_ordinal":102,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The lemma declares h as a unary real function, and both the preceding addition map and the following three-variable integrand require composition h(w+u), not an undefined binary h(w,u).","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt274.tex:195-197","source_normalized_sha256":"17e7d3c7b758bf4555573acfe2dc62fc54cc8b5ba9398ddef80cded97dcf181b","source_text":"$(w,u)\\mapsto h(w,u)$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt274.tex:193-195","target_normalized_sha256":"a13dce2a9667ca0dab5281fc30aba3f862dde9a32ded09cbce1058a8972f0f58","target_text":"$(w,u)\\mapsto h(w+u)$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S274"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-domain-extension","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0309","provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The lemma requires a function on all of R with the stated constant tails, but the proof only defined it on the closed transition interval; the constant extensions complete the construction and match the endpoint derivatives.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt274.tex:309-311","source_text":"for $|x|\\le\\epsilon$.","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt274.tex:310-312","target_normalized_sha256":"2c4d66f60a7d546f624f40aaa6ef64238709feab7867defa26b68ba4fd20b7b8","target_text":"$h(x)=1\\text{ jika }x\\le-\\epsilon,\\quad\\text{dan}\\quad h(x)=0\\text{ jika }x\\ge\\epsilon$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S274"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-translated-function-subscript","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0310","math_ordinal":239,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"This paragraph states derivative bounds for the translate h_t; the second bound must name h_t just as the preceding h_t double-prime bound does.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt274.tex:445-447","source_normalized_sha256":"dd011b751a2083b09a6017bf8dc1e64f60ceace057f73b996d3fcde302907205","source_text":"$\\sup_{x\\in\\Bbb R}|h'''(x)|=M_3$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt274.tex:440-442","target_normalized_sha256":"d3757114ea4fc0736c11999dbedecaeb77ae21784d05e59a2d6c0883360e02a4","target_text":"$\\sup_{x\\in\\Bbb R}|h_t'''(x)|=M_3$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S274"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-indicator-endpoint","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0311","math_ordinal":244,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The middle indicator is the same left-tail distribution event as the two surrounding indicators; an interval beginning at positive infinity is empty and breaks the sandwich.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt274.tex:470-472","source_normalized_sha256":"9492323b614e2117069129a22d4d75f489d907e4434c54570f5edc023d3e5805","source_text":"$\\chi\\ocint{-\\infty,a-2\\epsilon}\\le h_{a-\\epsilon}\\le\\chi\\ocint{\\infty,a}\\le h_{a+\\epsilon}\\le\\chi\\ocint{-\\infty,a+\\epsilon}$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt274.tex:465-467","target_normalized_sha256":"d63350dd547b686bcca11de6fb99f45e5cf976849e14137dd962ff26e1d14618","target_text":"$\\chi\\ocint{-\\infty,a-2\\epsilon}\\le h_{a-\\epsilon}\\le\\chi\\ocint{-\\infty,a}\\le h_{a+\\epsilon}\\le\\chi\\ocint{-\\infty,a+\\epsilon}$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S274"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-normalization-index","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0312","math_ordinal":324,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The proof defines s_n=sigma sqrt(n+1) immediately above, so expanding psi_{epsilon s_n} requires the same n+1 threshold.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt274.tex:646-647","source_normalized_sha256":"e667c1fdcf81f1220cebc3033947fd826688bb07f5e9fd754983b9ebe11cf71a","source_text":"\\int_{\\{x:|x|>\\epsilon\\sigma\\sqrt{n}\\}}x^2\\nu(dx)","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt274.tex:638-639","target_normalized_sha256":"a7c072095e75f3b9be6abec5d37e0fc5250bce9c8184f521eff1ddf51a73e10b","target_text":"\\int_{\\{x:|x|>\\epsilon\\sigma\\sqrt{n+1}\\}}x^2\\nu(dx)","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S274"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-centering","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0313","math_ordinal":471,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"For common expectation c, the uncentered normalized sum has expectation c sqrt(n+1) and cannot converge to N(c,sigma^2). Centering each summand and adding c yields exactly the asserted limiting mean and variance.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt274.tex:880-885","source_normalized_sha256":"b727d236b4da2452e966c484048068283989ed461e1322b176f9326ca76d6195","source_text":"$S_n=\\Bover1{\\sqrt{n+1}}(X_0+\\ldots+X_n)$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt274.tex:868-873","target_normalized_sha256":"367dc2e6c4df7e7991e7695ca8b21a8fd528d711b32e0554262c1e5a00197c19","target_text":"$S_n=c+\\Bover1{\\sqrt{n+1}}\\sum_{i=0}^n(X_i-c)$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S274"}
{"classification":"mathematical-stray-delimiter","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0314","math_ordinal":505,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The final closing parenthesis has no opening mate and lies outside the probability expression; removing it restores the intended one-half lower bound.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt274.tex:932-935","source_normalized_sha256":"cc2758cce32dca5279a2d4f39b4d8d076d29bc5463cab8140e3c11bf87c8cfd7","source_text":"$\\lim_{m\\to\\infty}\\Pr(|\\sum_{i=n}^mt_iX_i|\\ge 1)\\ge\\bover12)$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt274.tex:921-924","target_normalized_sha256":"34b2c0ff960704ce8a1e9c494efb4999dcf72dfa201b626cd20499b81b941429","target_text":"$\\lim_{m\\to\\infty}\\Pr(|\\sum_{i=n}^mt_iX_i|\\ge 1)\\ge\\bover12$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S274"}
{"classification":"mathematical-impossible-indicator-sandwich","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0315","math_ordinal":531,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"At x below -epsilon the lower indicator is one while the printed upper right-tail indicator is zero, making the inequalities impossible. The upper indicator must be the left tail through epsilon, as in Lemma 274E.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt274.tex:963-965","source_normalized_sha256":"a375fdfab323bcb69cd1ebaaab76e6a6ba313c53f59485151a78b93759880fce","source_text":"$\\chi\\ocint{-\\infty,-\\epsilon}\\le h\\le\\chi\\coint{\\epsilon,\\infty}$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt274.tex:953-955","target_normalized_sha256":"32b9e68022fee910167a85453f4d579f5f237e13e839d233ed61c5f5909e9d9b","target_text":"$\\chi\\ocint{-\\infty,-\\epsilon}\\le h\\le\\chi\\ocint{-\\infty,\\epsilon}$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S274"}
